text:
if you’ve finished all rain world campaigns, including dlc and mods, and want even more content to be released, I humbly suggest living in the real world for a while
//////
Me from like a month later; needed to take my own fucking advice lmao

I just had a flash of a vision where I die young, and people comment on how often I talked about death and age and stuff considering I died so young. I don’t believe it will happen, and I don’t think they’d talk that way about it anyway lol
//////
I didn’t even finish the original point I was trying to get to with this memory. I feel that I am passing a threshhold, beyond which my memory of my childhood and early adolesence will be too cloudy for me to write about and remember accurately. I want to record all that before I forget it and no longer can.

Our thoughts are always only in orbit around what we actually mean. So too do the patterns in life only orbit around the core of what’s really happening.
//////
Why are these repeat thoughts recorded anyway, why do they not stay, and why do I continue to write? Because the way in which I came to the realization again is why I was struck, not the realization itself.

Parents see children playing in the rain and say shit like “why don’t you get excited about taking a shower like that”
/////
Oh. I think the insurmountable distance between me and my father started when he threw away my blue hat.

There is a certain type of writerly, worldly connection I have when writing coming up to a high (at least, in the content of what I experience; the translated words and typed sentences you see at the end of all of it is a little iffy. Example: See previous entry. What a mess, despite how profound a points I truly felt, and was trying to make) that I don’t have often when sober. There is a certain vividness and color that I find “feels like” the most natural I ever am in how bare I am able to touch the world with my mind and emotions. I feel raw in an intimate way with the world around me.
//////
I am somehow missing an entire entry. I know I did not call the Family Fart entry “profound”.

If you like my writing I probably don’t want to talk to you. I wonder what emotion made me think that. Because it wasn’t pride.
//////
It was simple ignorance.
